:"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Zevachim 36b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_36b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"וכ\"ה בבה\"ז","reason":"Kaidanover’s Birkat Ha-Zevah is bibliographically identified as a commentary on Kodashim. The checked folio transcriptions do not supply a matching comment on 31b, and digital commentary access did not verify Heilprin’s reading. Retain provisional expansion and hold the exact locus.","evidence":[]}],"notes":[{"text":"The checked Menahot 15b reads Rabbi Abba Zuti. Heilprin names Rava Zuti. Zevahim 24a shows Zuti reframing R. Ammi’s question. The unsuccessful Zevahim 36a identification and the precise Birkat Ha-Zevah locus are left unlinked.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Zevachim 24a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_24a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Zevachim 24a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_24a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Menachot 15b:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_15b.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
